            model: "The Marshall-Lerner condition states that a depreciation improves the current account if the sum of the price elasticities of demand for exports and imports exceeds 1. Here 0.4 + 0.5 = 0.9, which is less than 1, so export volumes rise and import volumes fall too little to offset the lower export prices and dearer imports - the current account balance is likely to worsen.",
